diff -ruN v0120_phase20_base/PLANNING_PORTAL_FALLBACK.md v0120_phase20_work/PLANNING_PORTAL_FALLBACK.md
--- v0120_phase20_base/PLANNING_PORTAL_FALLBACK.md	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ v0120_phase20_work/PLANNING_PORTAL_FALLBACK.md	2026-08-05 20:30:00.000000000 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Planning portal fallback
+
+Phase 20 recovers planning applications from bounded local-authority portal pages when the national Planning Data feed contains no `planning-application` records for the requested park.
+
+## Current provider
+
+The built-in Staffordshire Moorlands provider is activated only for the Alton Towers preset/name or a bounding box intersecting the configured authority area. It inspects the council's bounded major-applications register and retains only rows matching Alton Towers or Farley Lane.
+
+The provider registry is intentionally data-driven so more authorities can be added without changing document classification or planning-authority fusion.
+
+## Safety boundary
+
+Portal fallback:
+
+- fetches only explicitly configured seed pages;
+- follows only application links found on those pages;
+- applies the existing application and document caps;
+- does not submit search forms, authenticate, bypass access controls, or crawl unrelated pages;
+- leaves downloaded documents cache-only when no reuse licence is declared;
+- never changes the world directly.
+
+## Legacy attachment compatibility
+
+Legacy `AttachmentShowServlet?ImageName=...` links are treated as downloadable candidates even when the URL has no file extension. The downloaded bytes must still pass MIME sniffing before they are accepted.
+
+## Geometry extraction queue
+
+Downloaded site, block, landscape, ride, access, terrain, floor, elevation, section, and lighting drawings are added to `geometryExtractionQueue` in `planning-document-catalogue.json`.
+
+Each queue entry records:
+
+- application reference and decision status;
+- document role and revision state;
+- source URL, hash, MIME type, and byte count;
+- reuse status;
+- an initial confidence hint;
+- `awaiting-georeference` status.
+
+This queue is the handoff to the next georeferencing/vectorisation stage. It is evidence only and cannot replace OSM until generated GeoJSON passes the existing Phase 18 implementation, confidence, overlap, displacement, and ambiguity gates.
+
+## Alton Towers result
+
+For an Alton Towers build, the fallback can recover historical major applications including rollercoasters, indoor attractions, accommodation, paths, landscaping, drainage, parking, and associated buildings that are absent from the national Planning Data response.
+
+The build diagnostics report the provider, seed pages fetched, matched applications, rejected rows, portal failures, and geometry queue size.
